## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- **Python 3.11+** → [Download](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
- **Node.js 18+** → [Download](https://nodejs.org/)
- **Git** → [Download](https://git-scm.com/)
- **OpenAI API Key** (optional) → [Get Key](https://platform.openai.com/api-keys)

> 💡 **No API key? No problem!** The app runs in **mock mode** with simulated LLM responses.

---

### 🔧 Backend Setup

```bash
# 1. Navigate to backend
cd backend

# 2. Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# 3. Activate virtual environment
# Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# Mac/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

# 4. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 5. Setup environment variables
copy .env.example .env       # Windows
# cp .env.example .env       # Mac/Linux

# 6. Edit .env and add your OpenAI key (optional)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# 7. Run the server
python run.py
Backend runs at: http://localhost:8000
API Docs (Swagger): http://localhost:8000/docs

🎨 Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal:

bash
# 1. Navigate to frontend
cd frontend

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Start dev server
npm run dev
Frontend runs at: http://localhost:5173

📖 How It Works
1️⃣ User Inputs Negotiation Parameters
text
Item: Enterprise Cloud Servers
Quantity: 50
Buyer Budget: $120,000
Seller Asking: $180,000
Deadline: 30 days
Quality: High
2️⃣ Multi-Agent Debate (3 Rounds)
Round 1:

🟢 Buyer Agent → Proposes low price, cites budget constraints

🔴 Seller Agent → Counters with value justification

Round 2:

🟢 Buyer Agent → Adjusts offer upward slightly

🔴 Seller Agent → Offers discount with conditions

Round 3:

🔵 Mediator Agent → Analyzes both sides

3️⃣ Constraint Optimization
Linear Programming solver finds optimal price satisfying:

✅ Price ≤ Buyer Budget

✅ Price ≥ Seller Floor (60% asking)

✅ Quality penalty weights

✅ Deadline penalty weights

4️⃣ Final Deal
text
✅ Final Price: $142,500
📦 Quantity: 50
🚚 Delivery: 30 days
⭐ Quality: High
💳 Payment: 30% advance, 70% on delivery
🛡️ Warranty: 12 months
🔌 API Endpoints
Negotiations
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/negotiations/	Create new negotiation
GET	/api/negotiations/	List all negotiations
GET	/api/negotiations/{id}	Get negotiation detail
DELETE	/api/negotiations/{id}	Delete negotiation
History & Stats
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/history/stats	Get overall statistics
Example Request
bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/negotiations/ \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "Cloud Server Procurement",
    "item": "Enterprise Cloud Servers",
    "quantity": 50,
    "buyer_budget": 120000,
    "seller_asking_price": 180000,
    "deadline_days": 30,
    "quality_requirement": "high"
  }'
Example Response
json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Cloud Server Procurement",
  "status": "completed",
  "final_price": 142500.00,
  "final_terms": "Final Price: $142500.00\nQuantity: 50\n...",
  "rounds": [
    {
      "round_number": 1,
      "agent": "Buyer",
      "message": "Given my budget constraints...",
      "proposed_price": 84000.00
    },
    {
      "round_number": 1,
      "agent": "Seller",
      "message": "Our costs are rising...",
      "proposed_price": 180000.00
    }
  ]
}
